1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:05,820
Right now your body is doing things you did not decide on.
You are blinking. Your heart is keeping time.

2
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:09,680
And at some point in the next hour your face will open and
you will yawn.

3
00:00:10,670 --> 00:00:13,486
Two thousand years ago somebody made a list of twelve
such things.

4
00:00:13,486 --> 00:00:17,880
Twelve acts a body performs without instruction. It is the
oldest catalogue of the involuntary we have,

5
00:00:17,880 --> 00:00:19,330
and it is stranger than it sounds.

6
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:23,377
Let the record show that this is a formal inquiry and not a
consultation.

7
00:00:23,377 --> 00:00:27,677
Twelve counts of insubordination committed inside my own
person, daily, for as long as I can remember.

8
00:00:27,677 --> 00:00:29,700
I intend to find out exactly who is responsible.

9
00:00:30,465 --> 00:00:35,819
Then I should tell you at the outset that your inquiry has a
difficulty. You have twelve offences and no offender at all.

10
00:00:35,819 --> 00:00:39,535
Nothing in this chapter decides to do any of it, and there is
no one here to charge.

11
00:00:40,895 --> 00:00:47,354
The book is the Spiritual Pivot, the practical half of the
Inner Canon. Chapter twenty-eight, Oral Inquiry.

12
00:00:47,354 --> 00:00:49,105
Twelve questions, no culprit.

13
00:00:50,845 --> 00:00:54,929
This is The Emperor's Inner Canon, and this episode is
called Twelve Small Rebellions.

14
00:00:54,929 --> 00:00:59,155
It is about the parts of you that are not taking orders, and
about who a body belongs to.

15
00:01:00,270 --> 00:01:03,606
Then we proceed differently. If no one is responsible, tell
me instead what is.

16
00:01:03,606 --> 00:01:08,379
Something opens my mouth against my wishes at the worst
possible moments in front of my court. It is not nothing.

17
00:01:08,379 --> 00:01:09,730
Name it and I will deal with it.

18
00:01:10,895 --> 00:01:14,825
Qi. Moving on a schedule it did not choose either. It goes
out at dawn and in at midnight,

19
00:01:14,825 --> 00:01:19,105
the way water goes downhill, and it is not obeying anyone
when it does. That is the entire answer.

20
00:01:20,740 --> 00:01:26,224
Hold on to that, because ten riddles later this same chapter
will announce that the heart is the ruler of all the organs.

21
00:01:26,224 --> 00:01:29,260
One book, two bodies. One of them governed, and one
simply running.

22
00:01:30,905 --> 00:01:35,753
Count one. When a person yawns, what qi brings it about? I
was mid-proclamation before the whole court,

23
00:01:35,753 --> 00:01:39,095
and my own face opened like a gate in a wall that nobody
was defending.

24
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:45,558
Defensive qi keeps a circuit. Through the daylight it runs in
the yang, at your surface, where the weather is.

25
00:01:45,558 --> 00:01:49,160
At midnight it goes down into the yin. Nobody sends it
there. It is simply the hour.

26
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:55,359
Yin governs the night, and the night is for lying down. Yang
governs what is above; yin governs what is below.

27
00:01:55,359 --> 00:01:59,290
Two rules about direction, and everything that follows is
built out of them and nothing else.

28
00:02:00,255 --> 00:02:05,510
Here is the mechanism. Yin qi has already gathered low in
you and yang qi has not yet finished its day.

29
00:02:05,510 --> 00:02:09,745
The yang draws upward while the yin draws downward, and
neither one of them yields.

30
00:02:10,280 --> 00:02:16,457
Yin and yang draw against one another, and therefore one
yawns, and yawns again. Read the verb: one yawns.

31
00:02:16,457 --> 00:02:19,720
It simply happens to you, and it happens in the passive.

32
00:02:20,340 --> 00:02:24,271
That is not an acquittal, that is an insult. You are telling me
that the sovereign of this realm,

33
00:02:24,271 --> 00:02:27,958
standing in front of forty ministers, was overruled by
weather moving through his own legs.

34
00:02:27,958 --> 00:02:29,660
There must be an appeal somewhere in this.

35
00:02:30,780 --> 00:02:35,236
There is no appeal, and there is also no insult in it. You
were not overruled. You were never consulted.

36
00:02:35,236 --> 00:02:39,220
A thing can only overrule you if it was ever taking
instructions from you in the first place.

37
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:45,659
When yang qi is spent and yin qi is full, the eyes close.
That is not a description of falling asleep.

38
00:02:45,659 --> 00:02:49,320
In this system it is the cause of falling asleep, and it uses
no new parts.

39
00:02:50,465 --> 00:02:55,145
And when yin qi is spent and yang qi is full, you wake. The
same two quantities, the same seesaw,

40
00:02:55,145 --> 00:02:59,535
simply read at the other end of the night. Nothing at all has
been added to explain either.

41
00:03:00,770 --> 00:03:06,733
Count what that bought. Yawning, falling asleep and waking
up, from one moving quantity and one rule about direction.

42
00:03:06,733 --> 00:03:09,230
One mechanism, and nobody in charge of any of it.

43
00:03:11,085 --> 00:03:13,003
May I put something in the record, since nobody has asked
me.

44
00:03:13,003 --> 00:03:15,582
I have yawned four times since we started and nobody
ordered me to do that either,

45
00:03:15,582 --> 00:03:18,915
so by the emperor's own reasoning I should be standing in
the dock beside him and not sitting at the back.

46
00:03:20,310 --> 00:03:24,733
Now the obvious question. Two thousand years on, with
sleep laboratories and brain imaging,

47
00:03:24,733 --> 00:03:29,690
why do we actually yawn? The honest position is that there
is still no agreed answer to that question.

48
00:03:30,770 --> 00:03:35,558
One proposal says a yawn marks a change of state. Not
tiredness but the hinge between sleep and waking,

49
00:03:35,558 --> 00:03:39,230
or between boredom and attention, and it is the best
supported of them we have.

50
00:03:40,535 --> 00:03:44,740
Then note what this chapter had already claimed, two
thousand years before anyone could measure anything.

51
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:47,062
The yawn belongs to the hinge between sleeping and
waking.

52
00:03:47,062 --> 00:03:49,465
It placed the yawn where the modern account still places it.

53
00:03:50,275 --> 00:03:53,605
Right about when. Wrong about why. Keep those two scores
well apart,

54
00:03:53,605 --> 00:03:57,375
because we will be marking them separately eleven more
times in this episode,

55
00:03:57,375 --> 00:03:59,725
and they never once merge into a single verdict.

56
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:06,209
And there is a second score, which is the one this episode
is really keeping. Every answer so far has had no author.

57
00:04:06,209 --> 00:04:09,635
Nothing decided, nothing chose. Watch carefully how long
that holds.

58
00:04:11,015 --> 00:04:13,715
It holds for nine more of them. I will take those nine
quickly,

59
00:04:13,715 --> 00:04:16,028
because the interest is not in any single one of them.

60
00:04:16,028 --> 00:04:18,985
The interest is that not one of them has anybody at all at
the wheel.

61
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:23,854
Nine more. Which leaves two, and those two must have
somebody at the wheel,

62
00:04:23,854 --> 00:04:25,784
and I would very much like to be given his name.

63
00:04:25,784 --> 00:04:29,160
So far this inquiry has produced no defendant at all and a
great deal of philosophy.

64
00:04:30,595 --> 00:04:34,227
He is right that there are two of them, and he is going to
wish very much that there were not,

65
00:04:34,227 --> 00:04:38,478
because the two counts that do have an author are the two
that hurt, and the author this chapter names is him,

66
00:04:38,478 --> 00:04:39,405
and he already knows it.

67
00:04:40,965 --> 00:04:45,519
Nine riddles, and I am going to move quickly through all of
them, because the point is not any one of them at all.

68
00:04:45,519 --> 00:04:49,035
The point is a sentence you will hear nine times without a
single person anywhere in it.

69
00:04:50,395 --> 00:04:52,868
Count two. When a person hiccups, what qi brings it about?

70
00:04:52,868 --> 00:04:55,938
I ask because it happened during a formal audience with a
foreign envoy,

71
00:04:55,938 --> 00:04:59,605
and the man plainly found it a great deal funnier than the
treaty we had come to sign.

72
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:05,700
Grain enters the stomach. Stomach qi pours upward into the
lung. That is the ordinary traffic and it runs one way.

73
00:05:05,700 --> 00:05:09,450
Note that the grain is the subject of that sentence, and the
grain has no opinions.

74
00:05:11,045 --> 00:05:15,791
Now let old cold qi still be sitting there when the new grain
qi arrives. New and old fall into disorder,

75
00:05:15,791 --> 00:05:18,955
and the qi combine, run backwards, and leave again through
your mouth.

76
00:05:20,450 --> 00:05:24,691
Before you dismiss the stomach, note this. A stomach
stretched full really does set hiccups off,

77
00:05:24,691 --> 00:05:29,550
and the nerve that reports a full stomach passes the
diaphragm on its way. The organ was not picked at random.

78
00:05:30,355 --> 00:05:35,400
Careful. That is the trap this whole episode is about. A real
trigger, attributed to the wrong organ,

79
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:39,645
by a mechanism that does not exist. What a hiccup is for,
incidentally, nobody knows.

80
00:05:40,885 --> 00:05:45,539
Count three, the belch. Cold lodges as a guest in the
stomach, turns back, and comes out again.

81
00:05:45,539 --> 00:05:49,115
The same shape, and the same absence of anybody
deciding anything at all.

82
00:05:50,405 --> 00:05:54,481
Then the text does something strange. It gives its
treatment, and adds three characters: another says.

83
00:05:54,481 --> 00:05:56,319
A second opinion, incompatible with the first,

84
00:05:56,319 --> 00:05:59,595
set down without comment and without any attempt at all to
choose between the two.

85
00:06:00,590 --> 00:06:03,014
Those three characters appear three times in this chapter.

86
00:06:03,014 --> 00:06:06,400
Each time two teachers said different things and whoever
wrote it down kept both.

87
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:09,410
That is what oral transmission looks like when it finally
reaches paper.

88
00:06:10,460 --> 00:06:16,738
Count four, the sneeze, and it is the odd one out. Yang qi is
harmonious and running freely. It fills the heart.

89
00:06:16,738 --> 00:06:19,540
It issues from the nose. Hear what is not in that.

90
00:06:20,470 --> 00:06:22,709
May I ask about the sun, since we are on the subject of
sneezing.

91
00:06:22,709 --> 00:06:26,602
Every single time I walk out of this hall into bright daylight
I sneeze exactly twice and never once three times.

92
00:06:26,602 --> 00:06:29,530
My father does it and my sister does it too. Is that anywhere
in your list of twelve?

93
00:06:30,425 --> 00:06:36,314
It is not, and it is entirely real. Somewhere between a sixth
and a third of people sneeze on stepping into bright light.

94
00:06:36,314 --> 00:06:39,575
It runs in families, it is inherited, and the mechanism is
unknown.

95
00:06:40,625 --> 00:06:45,217
Count five, and I warn you it is unglamorous. When the
saliva runs down. Food and drink enter the stomach;

96
00:06:45,217 --> 00:06:49,375
if there is heat there, the worms stir; the stomach slackens;
the spring under the tongue opens.

97
00:06:50,515 --> 00:06:54,232
Worms, meant literally. Intestinal parasites were an
ordinary fact of life,

98
00:06:54,232 --> 00:06:59,485
reached for the way cold and wind are reached for. It is a
mechanism that is checkable and entirely wrong.

99
00:07:00,275 --> 00:07:02,746
Count six, and this one I have never asked anybody about.

100
00:07:02,746 --> 00:07:07,428
After a man has finished weeping his breath keeps catching
by itself, in small shudders that he cannot stop.

101
00:07:07,428 --> 00:07:09,725
What is that? Nothing at all seems to be deciding it.

102
00:07:11,070 --> 00:07:16,596
Yin qi is full and yang qi is thin. Yin moves quickly while
yang moves slowly, and yin floods until yang is cut off.

103
00:07:16,596 --> 00:07:18,930
And so the breath catches and will not level out.

104
00:07:20,925 --> 00:07:25,260
This one is disputed and we will say so. The character can
be read as shivering rather than sobbing,

105
00:07:25,260 --> 00:07:29,075
and one translation in circulation reads it that way. We
think that reading is mistaken.

106
00:07:30,765 --> 00:07:36,892
The reason is count seven, shivering, which has its own
answer. Cold qi lodges as a guest in the skin,

107
00:07:36,892 --> 00:07:39,235
yin is full and yang is thin. One line.

108
00:07:40,780 --> 00:07:46,306
Count eight. If the stomach is not full, the vessels are
empty. If the vessels are empty, the sinews go slack,

109
00:07:46,306 --> 00:07:49,220
and effort then spends something that cannot be paid back.

110
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:55,671
Count nine, and I have wanted to ask this one for years. At
night, when the whole palace has gone silent, my ears ring.

111
00:07:55,671 --> 00:07:59,320
There is nothing there and nobody else hears it. What is
making a noise inside my head?

112
00:08:00,695 --> 00:08:03,579
The ears, exactly like the eyes, are where the great
vessels gather.

113
00:08:03,579 --> 00:08:07,524
When the stomach is empty those vessels are depleted, and
being depleted they drain downward.

114
00:08:07,524 --> 00:08:09,305
Where a vessel has run dry, the ear rings.

115
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:15,580
That one is simply wrong and we will not soften it. Ringing
in the ears is generated in the hearing pathway,

116
00:08:15,580 --> 00:08:19,060
usually following damage further out. It has nothing to do
with an empty stomach.

117
00:08:20,705 --> 00:08:25,226
Count ten, and it is the one that has always bothered me
most. Sometimes a man bites his own tongue,

118
00:08:25,226 --> 00:08:29,295
and not carelessly. His own jaw and his own tongue, and
somehow he still ambushes himself.

119
00:08:30,865 --> 00:08:36,103
Qi turns back and runs upward, and the vessel qi arrives out
of turn. When shaoyin qi arrives you bite the tongue,

120
00:08:36,103 --> 00:08:39,135
and when shaoyang arrives it is the cheek. Each one has
its place.

121
00:08:40,685 --> 00:08:44,840
Wrong, and beautifully shaped. Biting your tongue is a
timing error between jaw and tongue.

122
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:49,315
But that is ten answers now, and not one of them has
contained a single person who chose anything.

123
00:08:51,010 --> 00:08:53,408
Two counts remain, and they are not like the other ten.

124
00:08:53,408 --> 00:08:56,548
The chapter has spent nine minutes describing a body that
nobody drives.

125
00:08:56,548 --> 00:08:58,990
It is about to hand the wheel to somebody in particular.

126
00:09:00,770 --> 00:09:07,205
Count eleven. When a man grieves, and water comes out of
his face, what qi is doing that?

127
00:09:07,205 --> 00:09:09,230
And where does it come from?

128
00:09:10,625 --> 00:09:16,116
Begin where the chapter begins. The heart is the ruler of the
five zang and the six fu. Not the largest, not the strongest.

129
00:09:16,116 --> 00:09:19,375
The one the others answer to. Everything after this depends
on that word.

130
00:09:20,730 --> 00:09:25,655
Stop there on that word. For ten answers running this
chapter has had no ruler in it anywhere,

131
00:09:25,655 --> 00:09:29,270
and qi moved because it was the hour. Now something is
giving orders.

132
00:09:30,375 --> 00:09:34,407
The eyes are where the great vessels gather, and they are
the road that fluid climbs.

133
00:09:34,407 --> 00:09:39,625
The mouth and nose are the gates of qi. A ruler and a road
and a pair of gates. Watch what grief does to them.

134
00:09:40,965 --> 00:09:45,401
Sorrow and grief and care and worry, and the heart is
moved. The heart being moved,

135
00:09:45,401 --> 00:09:49,035
all five zang and all six fu are shaken rather than merely
saddened.

136
00:09:50,930 --> 00:09:54,293
They being shaken, the great vessels respond. The vessels
responding,

137
00:09:54,293 --> 00:09:59,070
the fluid road opens and the tears come out of you. Six
links, and the first of them is a feeling.

138
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:05,111
The first link being a feeling is why this episode exists.
Ten answers where nothing was the cause,

139
00:10:05,111 --> 00:10:09,300
and now an answer where something is. The cause is grief,
and grief belongs to whoever has it.

140
00:10:10,665 --> 00:10:16,396
I have carried this fan eleven years and I am setting it on
the table. My mother died in the spring. I have not wept,

141
00:10:16,396 --> 00:10:19,335
not once, and I want to know whether the road in me is shut.

142
00:10:20,445 --> 00:10:25,920
The chapter does not answer that, and I will not pretend
otherwise. What it says next is this. Weep and do not stop,

143
00:10:25,920 --> 00:10:29,555
and the fluid is exhausted; the essence is not watered; the
eyes see nothing.

144
00:10:30,805 --> 00:10:34,708
It calls that the robbing of the essence. A beautiful phrase
fastened to a false claim:

145
00:10:34,708 --> 00:10:39,195
crying does not drain a finite supply, and weeping does not
take your eyesight. We say that plainly.

146
00:10:40,510 --> 00:10:47,449
Count twelve, the last of them, and the one the chapter gets
closest to right. When a person sighs the long breath out,

147
00:10:47,449 --> 00:10:49,490
what qi is it that brings it about?

148
00:10:50,515 --> 00:10:57,089
Worry and brooding draw the cords of the heart tight. The
cords tight, the road of qi narrows and does not run freely.

149
00:10:57,089 --> 00:10:59,485
And so one sighs, to stretch it open again.

150
00:11:00,990 --> 00:11:05,144
A spontaneous sigh reinflates parts of the lung that have
quietly collapsed and restores its stretch.

151
00:11:05,144 --> 00:11:09,010
A small cluster of cells in the brainstem exists to generate
them, every few minutes, all day.

152
00:11:11,025 --> 00:11:16,149
Something constricted, and a breath that opens it. Right
shape, right company, wrong organ. It is the lung,

153
00:11:16,149 --> 00:11:18,975
not the cords of the heart. The closest this chapter comes.

154
00:11:20,925 --> 00:11:22,605
I want to point at something that nobody has said yet.

155
00:11:22,605 --> 00:11:26,182
Both of the ones with somebody at the wheel are the ones
that are about feeling. Grief and worry, and nothing else.

156
00:11:26,182 --> 00:11:29,075
Everything else in your twelve is weather of one kind or
another, and those two are a person.

157
00:11:30,735 --> 00:11:35,747
Which puts you in an awkward position, since you convened
an inquiry. Ten of your counts have no defendant at all.

158
00:11:35,747 --> 00:11:39,265
The other two do have one, and you have been sitting in his
chair all afternoon.

159
00:11:40,350 --> 00:11:45,455
So the body in this chapter is ungoverned for ten of its
twelve acts, and governed for the other two.

160
00:11:45,455 --> 00:11:49,650
That is not a small inconsistency. It is two theories of a
person, in one document.

161
00:11:50,975 --> 00:11:56,675
And then the chapter sums. All these twelve, it says, are
strange qi running into the hollow openings of the body.

162
00:11:56,675 --> 00:11:59,025
One sentence, gathering all of it into a claim.

163
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:03,786
Twelve. I counted them on the board as they came, and it
does come to twelve exactly,

164
00:12:03,786 --> 00:12:07,464
with none of them left over and none of them counted twice.
I would like that entered in the record,

165
00:12:07,464 --> 00:12:09,340
because I was told to sit at the back and be quiet.

166
00:12:10,510 --> 00:12:15,444
Then one more clause, and it is the sentence the chapter
has been walking toward from the beginning.

167
00:12:15,444 --> 00:12:19,490
Wherever the trouble is, in every case something is missing
rather than in excess.

168
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:23,590
And at that exact moment it splits. Go back six minutes.

169
00:12:23,590 --> 00:12:28,306
The sneeze was explained by qi being harmonious and
abundant. That is not something missing,

170
00:12:28,306 --> 00:12:29,280
and nobody notices.

171
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:35,609
That is the small seam, and here is the large one. Ten of
the twelve are explained with nobody at all in charge,

172
00:12:35,609 --> 00:12:39,260
and then the eleventh opens by installing a ruler over the
whole body, which is new.

173
00:12:40,620 --> 00:12:41,938
And it is not an isolated slip.

174
00:12:41,938 --> 00:12:46,786
Another chapter of this same canon builds the entire body
as a government of twelve offices with a sovereign and a

175
00:12:46,786 --> 00:12:49,380
chancellor and a general. Nothing happens without an
officer.

176
00:12:50,880 --> 00:12:56,080
One canon, two bodies. In one, you are an administration
and every act has an office responsible for it. In the other,

177
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:59,120
you are weather on a schedule, and twelve things a day
simply happen.

178
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:04,239
Before anyone feels superior, the modern position is not
tidier. It is messier.

179
00:13:04,239 --> 00:13:09,300
There is no single system running the involuntary, and the
twelve on this list do not share one mechanism either.

180
00:13:10,665 --> 00:13:15,177
The chapter's real error is not that it guessed wrong twelve
times. It is that it expected one answer.

181
00:13:15,177 --> 00:13:19,335
The involuntary is not a department. It is a dozen unrelated
things that happen to look alike.

182
00:13:20,850 --> 00:13:23,332
Which leaves the question the inquiry was convened to
answer,

183
00:13:23,332 --> 00:13:26,505
and it is a much better question than the emperor knew
when he first asked it.

184
00:13:26,505 --> 00:13:29,150
Who exactly is supposed to be in charge of you and of your
parts?

185
00:13:30,960 --> 00:13:34,476
I convened this inquiry to find a culprit. I have ten offences
with nobody at all behind them,

186
00:13:34,476 --> 00:13:36,234
and two behind which there is only me grieving,

187
00:13:36,234 --> 00:13:39,040
which is not a crime in any code that I have ever signed or
ever will sign.

188
00:13:41,090 --> 00:13:46,288
No. And here is the part I have been keeping back. A body
that needed a ruler for all twelve would be a worse body.

189
00:13:46,288 --> 00:13:48,910
Most of you runs without you, and that is the mercy in it.

190
00:13:51,090 --> 00:13:54,958
That is the chapter's genuine achievement, and it is easy
to miss under the wrong mechanisms.

191
00:13:54,958 --> 00:13:58,910
It looked at twelve things a body does unbidden and did not
once reach for a spirit or a fault.

192
00:14:01,050 --> 00:14:04,947
Eleven. That is how many times I have yawned since we
began this morning, and I counted every one of those too.

193
00:14:04,947 --> 00:14:08,950
Every one of them started because somebody else in this
room had just done it first, and not one of them was mine.

194
00:14:10,545 --> 00:14:15,162
He has found the one thing the chapter cannot hold.
Yawning is catching. It is documented in humans,

195
00:14:15,162 --> 00:14:19,455
in chimpanzees, and in dogs watching people, and the
mechanism behind it is entirely unknown.

196
00:14:20,335 --> 00:14:25,173
And no answer in this chapter can reach it. Every one of
them has a single body in it. One person,

197
00:14:25,173 --> 00:14:29,665
one set of channels. Catching a yawn takes two people, and
two people is not in the system.

198
00:14:30,870 --> 00:14:32,872
Then I withdraw the charges, all twelve of them,

199
00:14:32,872 --> 00:14:37,253
since it appears that I govern a great many things and that
the inside of my own mouth is not among them,

200
00:14:37,253 --> 00:14:39,130
and I am reliably told this is the good news.

201
00:14:40,685 --> 00:14:45,021
You have very likely yawned during the last fifteen
minutes, and nobody in the world can tell you why.

202
00:14:45,021 --> 00:14:49,315
An emperor put his own body on trial for it, and the verdict
was that there was nobody at all to try.

203
00:14:50,875 --> 00:14:54,391
A dramatized adaptation of a classical philosophical text.
Not medical advice.

204
00:14:54,391 --> 00:14:59,125
We present the Inner Canon as history and philosophy, and
we mark where the evidence does not support it.
